{
 "name": "Test room 7 — gravity",
 "notes": "Milestone 6. Walk into a gravity door and you are flipped onto the CEILING: your body stays put, gravity reverses and you fall up to the underside of the top slab, which is a second floor. Your pane turns upside down with you, so left/right keys follow your screen. Doors: \"up\" puts you on the ceiling, \"down\" back on the floor (a door only affects someone it can change, so you can walk on through it). ROOM: (A) a wall only passable along the ceiling; (B) a plate hanging from the ceiling opens the door on the floor — one of you holds it up there while the other goes through, then the holder drops down (the plate keeps the door open for 5s after you let go); (C) an 18-wide pit crossed on the ceiling, past a hanging block (jump it) and a fire jet at head height up there (with a gap before it to wait in); flags hang from the ceiling too; (D) the exit is on the ceiling, behind a door opened by a switch hanging from the ceiling. Shoulder carries work between two players on the ceiling but not between a floor player and a ceiling player. Dying sends you back to the last flag, the right way up for that flag.",
 "hint": "Gravity doors flip you onto the ceiling (it is a second floor; your view turns with you, left/right follow your screen). Wall: go along the ceiling. Plate on the ceiling: one holds it, one goes through, then drop down and follow. Pit: cross on the ceiling. The exit is up there.",
